# Clear Glass gig file (clearglass.gig/1) — load it in Settings → Autofill → Gig, or in the gig panel.
format: clearglass.gig/1
platform: fiverr
title: I will set up a private local AI on your PC with Ollama, no cloud
category: AI Services
subcategory: AI Development
serviceType: ''
tags:
  - ollama
  - local llm
  - private ai
  - ai setup
  - offline ai
description: >-
  Want AI that runs on your own computer, with your data never leaving it? I set up Ollama with the
  right models for your machine and your work, and show you how to use it.


  I run local models every day as part of my own AI system, routed beside cloud models, so I know
  which models fit which hardware and which jobs.


  What you get:

  - Ollama installed and tested on your Windows, Mac or Linux machine

  - Models picked for your RAM and graphics card, and for your task (writing, code, documents)

  - A simple chat interface, or a script that uses it from your own tools

  - A short guide: how to start it, switch models and keep it updated


  How it works: we start with what you want it for and what your computer has. I set it up remotely
  or with step-by-step instructions, then we test it together on a real task.


  Private by design: nothing goes to a cloud service unless you ask for it.
packages:
  basic:
    name: Install and Test
    description: Ollama and one model installed, tested, with a short guide.
    deliveryDays: 1
    revisions: 1
    price: 40
  standard:
    name: Tuned for Your Work
    description: Models chosen for your tasks, a chat interface and a guide.
    deliveryDays: 3
    revisions: 2
    price: 100
  premium:
    name: Local AI in Your Tools
    description: A script or small app that uses your local model in your workflow.
    deliveryDays: 6
    revisions: 3
    price: 250
faq:
  - question: Will it run on my computer?
    answer: >-
      Send me your RAM, graphics card and operating system. I will tell you honestly which models
      will run well before you order.
  - question: Is it really private?
    answer: >-
      Yes. The models run on your machine. Nothing is sent online unless you add a cloud service
      yourself.
  - question: Do you need remote access?
    answer: Not required. I can guide you step by step, or connect remotely if you prefer.
requirements:
  - What do you want the local AI to help with? (writing, code, documents, something else)
  - Who will use it, and on what? (Windows, Mac, a server; one person or a team)
  - What must it always do, and what must it never do?
  - How will you check that it is done? (the test you will run, or what you will look at)
  - Please share any files, examples, access or data I need to start.
metadata:
